+Exponential backoff with jitter can also take a floor and a cap, and accepts
+`datetime.timedelta` values as well as seconds.
+
+.. testcode::
+
+    import datetime
+
+    @retry(wait=wait_exponential_jitter(
+        initial=1,
+        min=datetime.timedelta(seconds=2),
+        max=datetime.timedelta(seconds=60),
+        jitter=datetime.timedelta(seconds=1),
+    ))
+    def wait_exponential_jitter_2_to_60_s():
+        print("Wait 2 to 60 seconds, growing exponentially, with up to 1 second of jitter")
+        raise Exception
+
 When multiple processes are in contention for a shared resource, exponentially
 increasing jitter helps minimise collisions.
 
